  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australia-Malaysia Institutional Strengthening Program (AMIS) is supporting Malaysia&#x2019;s efforts to strengthen public sector accountability through the establishment a Federal Ombudsman and Freedom of Information (FOI) legislation. Australia supported a delegation of senior government officials and civil society representatives to visit Australia in October 2024 to understand the functions and structure of Australia&#x2019;s Commonwealth Ombudsman and NSW Ombudsman. AMIS also supported several visits to Malaysia by former Commonwealth Ombudsman, Prof. John McMillan AO, to provide expert advice on best practices when structuring an Ombudsman&#x2019;s office and establishing FOI laws.  
&#x200d;
McMillan&#x2019;s multiagency consultations have informed Malaysia&#x2019;s draft Ombudsman Policy Paper and FOI Policy Paper, which are now under Cabinet consideration. These ongoing technical exchanges, at the request of the Legal Affairs Division in the Prime Minister&#x2019;s Department (BHEUU), will directly shape the final Ombudsman and FOI bills which are expected to be tabled in parliament by the end of 2025. By sharing expertise and supporting policy developments, Australia has made a significant contribution to some of Malaysia&#x2019;s key institutional reforms.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australia-Malaysia Institutional Strengthening Program (AMIS) is supporting the Malaysian Government to establish its first federal Freedom of Information (FOI) Act to improve government transparency. AMIS funded a delegation of Members of Parliament, government officials leading the drafting of the new legislation, and NGO representatives, to visit Australia in February 2024 to learn about Australia&#x2019;s FOI legislation, its implementation by government agencies, and the role of independent oversight mechanisms. Upon return to Malaysia, AMIS also supported the participation of NGOs in government-led stakeholder consultations in six Malaysian states to discuss the proposed FOI bill and ensure stakeholder buy-in. These activities have informed Malaysia&apos;s FOI bill, which is currently being drafted and is set to be tabled in the Malaysian Parliament in December 2024.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Malaysia-Australia Food Safety Cooperation project funded capacity building activities for Malaysian food safety officials over two phases. Firstly, in August-September 2023, Food Standards Australia New Zealand (FSANZ) conducted a six-day virtual workshop with officials from Malaysia&#x2019;s Ministry of Health (MoH) on food safety and microbiological risk analysis. Then, over 10 days in February-March 2024, the project funded two officers from MoH to attend in-person technical training on microbiological risk testing at Australia&#x2019;s National Measurement Institute in Sydney. The project helped to improve regulatory cooperation and harmonisation between Malaysia and Australia and by, improving overall food safety in Malaysia, can help to improve the trade in prepared foodstuffs between Malaysia and Australia.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
